WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
Your neighbor smokes on the balcony below.

2
00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.930
The smoke drifts up
through your open window.

3
00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.920
You never bought those cigarettes.

4
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.960
You still breathe the smoke.

5
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.990
In the US, secondhand smoke
causes more than 41,000

6
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.940
deaths a year among nonsmoking adults.

7
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.460
So when a product harms people
nearby who never bought it,

8
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.800
why does the market sell too much?

9
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.140
In this mission, you'll draw the
private benefit and the social

10
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.680
benefit as two separate curves.

11
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.620
Then you'll turn up the harm in a graph

12
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.710
lab and test your prediction.

13
00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:36.160
Your mission: find out why
the market sells too much,

14
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.000
and where the socially
optimal quantity really is.
